, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Post-rollback: service healthy, error rate 0.2%. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 regression and why it was promoted despite failing in staging.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 16521, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PPtuuQCKtsaCR6a7njKZ1v", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 16521, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PPtuuQCKtsaCR6a7njKZ1v", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20882, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **What went wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the newest release that was healthy in production. The test version (v2.3.1-rc) only ran in staging, and it failed there too, so it couldn't be used. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It also lists two things to look into: what broke in v2.3.1, and why it reached production even though its test version failed in staging.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01DE59ESPnyQ3vaUtVURK3jU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "to