ll regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **What went wrong:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the newest release that was healthy in production. The test version (v2.3.1-rc) only ran in staging, and it failed there too, so it couldn't be used. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate has dropped to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery, and the on-call engineer has been paged. It also lists two things to look into: what broke in v2.3.1, and why it reached production even though its test version failed in staging.", "type": "text"}]}]}